1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,585
The Curiosity Club.

2
00:00:02,585 --> 00:00:04,886
Episode 4.

3
00:00:04,886 --> 00:00:07,656
The Mystery Humming Box.

4
00:00:07,656 --> 00:00:10,681
Here is something to listen for.

5
00:00:10,681 --> 00:00:15,369
What happened when Maya gently stopped the rubber band from moving?

6
00:00:15,369 --> 00:00:16,960
Ready?

7
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:19,161
Let us find out.

8
00:00:19,161 --> 00:00:23,025
A strange humming sound comes from the music room.

9
00:00:23,025 --> 00:00:26,122
Maya stops outside the door.

10
00:00:26,122 --> 00:00:29,332
Is someone singing inside a box?

11
00:00:29,332 --> 00:00:31,505
Leo listens.

12
00:00:31,505 --> 00:00:35,482
It sounds like a very small monster with a cold.

13
00:00:35,482 --> 00:00:37,741
They knock and enter.

14
00:00:37,741 --> 00:00:43,707
Their music teacher is holding an empty tissue box with rubber bands stretched around it.

15
00:00:43,707 --> 00:00:47,002
Meet my new instrument, she says.

16
00:00:47,002 --> 00:00:49,630
Pip looks into the box.

17
00:00:49,630 --> 00:00:52,258
No monster detected.

18
00:00:52,258 --> 00:00:55,681
The teacher gently plucks a rubber band.

19
00:00:55,681 --> 00:01:00,198
It moves back and forth so quickly that its middle looks blurry.

20
00:01:00,198 --> 00:01:03,721
The box makes a soft musical sound.

21
00:01:03,721 --> 00:01:07,741
That movement is called vibration, she explains.

22
00:01:07,741 --> 00:01:12,031
The moving band makes the air around it vibrate, too.

23
00:01:12,031 --> 00:01:14,957
Maya touches the band gently.

24
00:01:14,957 --> 00:01:18,423
The movement stops, and the sound stops.

25
00:01:18,423 --> 00:01:21,207
Leo tries a tighter band.

26
00:01:21,207 --> 00:01:23,835
It makes a higher sound.

27
00:01:23,835 --> 00:01:27,187
He tries again, listening carefully.

28
00:01:27,187 --> 00:01:29,502
Can we play a song?

29
00:01:29,502 --> 00:01:31,747
Maya asks.

30
00:01:31,747 --> 00:01:36,903
You can try, says the teacher, but first listen to the notes you have.

31
00:01:36,903 --> 00:01:39,985
Their first song is not beautiful.

32
00:01:39,985 --> 00:01:43,693
Pip calls it A Robot Falling Down the Stairs.

33
00:01:43,693 --> 00:01:46,448
Their second song is better.

34
00:01:46,448 --> 00:01:50,639
Maya hums along and puts a hand lightly on her throat.

35
00:01:50,639 --> 00:01:53,480
She feels a tiny movement.

36
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:56,633
My voice makes vibrations, too!

37
00:01:56,633 --> 00:01:59,289
Pip records the concert.

38
00:01:59,289 --> 00:02:06,022
He saves it under Music, then thinks for a moment and adds a second label: Very Interesting Noise.

39
00:02:06,022 --> 00:02:09,176
Now, a little more to discover.

40
00:02:09,176 --> 00:02:12,144
Sound begins with vibration.

41
00:02:12,144 --> 00:02:18,053
Moving objects can make nearby air vibrate, and those changes travel to our ears.

42
00:02:18,053 --> 00:02:21,988
Vocal folds in your throat vibrate when you speak.

43
00:02:21,988 --> 00:02:28,039
A tighter string usually makes a higher note when its other important features stay the same.

44
00:02:28,039 --> 00:02:31,207
Let us hear the main idea again.

45
00:02:31,207 --> 00:02:35,369
The mystery sound came from a rubber-band instrument.

46
00:02:35,369 --> 00:02:39,389
When the band vibrated, the children heard a note.

47
00:02:39,389 --> 00:02:43,125
When Maya stopped the movement, the note stopped.

48
00:02:43,125 --> 00:02:47,769
They discovered that their own voices involve vibration, too.

49
00:02:47,769 --> 00:02:50,909
Here are three useful expressions.

50
00:02:50,909 --> 00:02:54,090
You can listen, or say them with me.

51
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:56,250
What can you hear?

52
00:02:56,250 --> 00:02:58,409
What can you hear?

53
00:02:58,409 --> 00:03:00,696
The room is noisy.

54
00:03:00,696 --> 00:03:02,982
The room is noisy.

55
00:03:02,982 --> 00:03:05,411
I can feel it moving.

56
00:03:05,411 --> 00:03:07,840
I can feel it moving.

57
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:10,838
Remember our listening question?

58
00:03:10,838 --> 00:03:15,525
What happened when Maya gently stopped the rubber band from moving?

59
00:03:15,525 --> 00:03:17,812
Here is the answer.

60
00:03:17,812 --> 00:03:22,684
The sound stopped because the rubber band was no longer vibrating.

61
00:03:22,684 --> 00:03:26,647
And here is a question just for your imagination.

62
00:03:26,647 --> 00:03:30,639
Which objects around you vibrate when they make a sound?

63
00:03:30,639 --> 00:03:33,948
There is more than one possible answer.

64
00:03:33,948 --> 00:03:37,244
Keep wondering, and see you next time.
